// The ways of walking players can pick from, under Player, Player Appearance, Walking Style.
//
// The name on the left is the clip set the game loads. The text on the right is what players see on
// the row, so write it however you like.
//
// You can add your own. Anything on this list is passed straight to the game, so a clip set your
// server streams itself works exactly like one that ships with GTA.
//
// A word of warning about which peds these suit. A clip set is animation, and animation is made for
// one shape of skeleton. The move_m@ ones were made for men, the move_f@ ones for women, and none of
// them were made for a dog. vMenu will let a player try any of them on any ped, and if the game has
// nothing to load it says so rather than pretending it worked. So feel free to offer everything and
// let people find out what looks right.
//
// Players always get a "Normal" choice on top of this list, which puts back the walk their ped came
// with. You do not need to add it yourself.
{
  // Men
  "move_m@casual@a": "休闲",
  "move_m@business@a": "商务",
  "move_m@tough_guy@": "硬汉",
  "move_m@gangster@a": "黑帮",
  "move_m@posh@": "优雅",
  "move_m@hipster@a": "潮人",
  "move_m@brave": "勇敢",
  "move_m@sad@a": "悲伤",
  "move_m@drunk@a": "微醉",
  "move_m@drunk@verydrunk": "烂醉",
  "move_m@injured": "受伤",
  "move_m@hurry@a": "匆忙",
  "move_m@money": "阔绰",

  // Women
